    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200:\n- The two halves of a partial method get two ids; explicit interface implementations (`void IA.F()` and `void IB.F()`) tie (MOVES IDS if fixed).\n- Tuple element NAMES are hashed (`(int a, int b)` differs from `(int x, int y)`): owner's call whether they should be.\n- Delegates, local functions and record primary-constructor parameters emit no symbol.\n- `_extract_param_types` (meta) skips the parameter kinds PR #2200 taught the hashed renderer.\n\nFixing a part marked MOVES IDS changes hashed input, so it belongs to the next stable-id bump, with a measured churn figure in the spec's history row.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # f410
